                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>President Truman, in reply to a question at his press conference of April 22,
                    1948, concerning the possible sending of American troops to Palestine, stated:
                    “We offered to furnish our share of a United Nations police force. That is the
                    only way we will send troops anywhere under the United Nations. As a part of a
                    United Nations police force for the enforcement of the orders of the United
                    Nations, we will furnish our share, just as Mr. Austin said we would.” (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents of the United States:
                        Harry S. Truman, 1948</hi>, page 229.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
